Package: GWPR.light
Type: Package
Title: Geographically Weighted Panel Regression
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(person("Chao", "Li", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                     email = "chaoli0394@gmail.com",
                     comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6854-4456")),
              person("Shunsuke", "Managi", role = "aut",
                     comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7883-1427")))
Description: A modern, sf-first implementation of Geographically Weighted Panel
    Regression (GWPR) for spatial panel data. The package provides a unified
    public API (gwpr(), select_bandwidth(), fit_gwpr(), diagnose_gwpr()) supporting
    Gaussian and binomial family models, within/pooling/random panel effects,
    three bandwidth search strategies (grid, SGD, random), five kernel functions,
    and optional parallel execution via the future framework. Diagnostic tools
    include spatial Moran's I, local F-test, Hausman test, and Lagrange Multiplier
    test. The major references are Fotheringham et al. (2003,
    ISBN:978-0-470-85525-6) and Beenstock and Felsenstein (2019,
    ISBN:978-3-030-03614-0).
